# Close-out B3 (M2-G2): a job that keeps failing real SMTP attempts is moved to failed/attempts_exhausted exactly at job_max_failed_attempts (default 6), in the same guarded UPDATE that would have requeued it. The fault disables the cap (the failed-attempt predicate is evaluated with counts=FALSE, so no failure is ever the Nth). The real claim -> handoff -> outcome path is driven with a persistent 554: five failures must leave the job queued, the sixth must end it. The unpatched control passes every step; the patched run stays queued at the sixth and the test says so. Module 2's DB tests need a migrated template database, so the CMD builds one on the stock postgres service first, as tests/harness/run.sh does.
GATE=m2-attempt-cap
TARGET=module:coldmail-send-managed
SETUP=
STEP=go test TestAttemptCap_FailedExactlyAtTheCap (a persistent 554 reaches failed/attempts_exhausted at exactly the cap, real Postgres)
CMD=T=fp_m2_p2c_tpl; TPL="${FAULT_ADMIN_DSN%/*}/$T"; psql "$FAULT_ADMIN_DSN" -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -q -c "DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS $T" -c "CREATE DATABASE $T" && psql "$TPL" -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -q -c "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.users(id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(), email text, is_active boolean default true, created_at timestamptz default now())" -c "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.job_items(id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(), campaign_id uuid, user_id uuid, recipient_email text, rendered_subject text, rendered_body text, reply_to text, status text, created_at timestamptz default now())" && (cd tools/send-managed-migrate && go build -o bin/send-managed-migrate .) && MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL="$TPL" SEND_MANAGED_MODULE_PASSWORD=devmodulepass tools/send-managed-migrate/bin/send-managed-migrate up-and-set-password && cd services/control && TEST_ADMIN_DATABASE_URL="$FAULT_ADMIN_DSN" TEST_TEMPLATE_DB="$T" SEND_MANAGED_MODULE_PASSWORD=devmodulepass go test -count=1 -v -run '^TestAttemptCap_FailedExactlyAtTheCap$' ./internal/dispatch/
MESSAGE=--- FAIL: TestAttemptCap_FailedExactlyAtTheCap
MESSAGE=want failed/attempts_exhausted, count=6
